From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] System.Drawing: resolve unspecified icon dimensions before selecting a frame.

Serialized Icon resources can contain IconSize = Size.Empty. Windows .NET
resolves each zero dimension to SM_CXICON / SM_CYICON before choosing an
image. Mono instead falls back to the largest non-ignored image by byte
count. SP Football Life 2026's Settings.exe consequently selects a damaged
48x48 image rather than one of its valid default-sized images and throws
"Unexpected number of bits: 0" while creating the form's window icon.

Resolve zero dimensions for stream loading (including deserialization)
and icon cloning. Reuse the existing User32 metrics binding on Windows;
retain the 32-pixel default on Unix. Leave explicit nonzero sizes, format
validation, and the frame selection algorithm otherwise unchanged.

Add generated multi-frame regression fixtures for zero dimensions,
empty/missing serialized sizes, a damaged unused frame, cloning, and
explicit larger sizes. No game assets or application-specific checks.

Reference for zero-size semantics:
https://github.com/dotnet/winforms/blob/main/src/System.Drawing.Common/src/System/Drawing/Icon.cs

Based on wine-mono/mono 775a29a0d864061a40438e38830c0afaadf9ae79
(Wine-Mono 11.2.0).
---
diff --git a/mcs/class/System.Drawing/System.Drawing/Icon.cs b/mcs/class/System.Drawing/System.Drawing/Icon.cs
--- a/mcs/class/System.Drawing/System.Drawing/Icon.cs
+++ b/mcs/class/System.Drawing/System.Drawing/Icon.cs
@@ -151,6 +151,7 @@
 			if (original == null)
 				throw new ArgumentException ("original");
 
+			size = ResolveIconSize (size.Width, size.Height);
 			iconSize = size;
 			iconDir = original.iconDir;
 			
@@ -736,12 +737,26 @@
 			Dispose ();
 		}
 			
+		private static Size ResolveIconSize (int width, int height)
+		{
+			// A zero dimension requests the system icon size, including in serialized resources.
+			if (width == 0)
+				width = GDIPlus.RunningOnWindows () ? UnsafeNativeMethods.GetSystemMetrics (SafeNativeMethods.SM_CXICON) : 32;
+			if (height == 0)
+				height = GDIPlus.RunningOnWindows () ? UnsafeNativeMethods.GetSystemMetrics (SafeNativeMethods.SM_CYICON) : 32;
+			return new Size (width, height);
+		}
